\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Hypervolume convergence of full vs MinPPI-prefiltered NSGA-II under the matched 800-evaluation budget. Each panel is a dataset; blue/green lines are five-seed means of cumulative-best validation hypervolume with $\pm $1-SD shading and reference point $(1.1,1.1)$. Curves coincide on most datasets and separate on Madelon; the dataset-averaged held-out change is +0.016{}. No dataset-wise comparison survives the registered Holm-corrected sign-flip tests.}}{7}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:prefilter}{{3}{7}{Hypervolume convergence of full vs MinPPI-prefiltered NSGA-II under the matched 800-evaluation budget. Each panel is a dataset; blue/green lines are five-seed means of cumulative-best validation hypervolume with $\pm $1-SD shading and reference point $(1.1,1.1)$. Curves coincide on most datasets and separate on Madelon; the dataset-averaged held-out change is \NsgaMeanHvChange {}. No dataset-wise comparison survives the registered Holm-corrected sign-flip tests}{figure.3}{}}
